nodes.body:
@xin-osaka-u Thanks for the quick fix — I checked c89d16c and the dtype guard + test look right to me. Good to know the Flash-Next NVFP4 checkpoint keeps its lm_head in BF16; that explains why this never surfaced on your side.

I agree with the "two designs fit different cases" framing and your arithmetic: on GB10-class unified memory the replicated head pays a real extra weight-read cost per rank (2x at your TP=2 numbers), while on HBM-class GPUs the extra read is cheap and the per-step gather is the larger collective. And for maps used as a hard restriction of the draft vocab (rather than just a size optimization), keeping the candidate set identical to TP=1 is the property worth paying for.

Same from my side — no preference on which lands, and both follow-up paths sound good (testing #43347 on GB10 TP=2, or layering the sharded layout as an option on top of it). Leaving the call to the maintainers.

